---
title: Interaction grammar
type: doc
---

::summary
The 0.47.0 interaction grammar on one adaptive shell: the shell's key chords
(the Mac's mod+1 to mod+5, mod+k and mod+w as source), a per-button key=,
a focus order on the seats and controls, a hover reveal with its keyboard
path, the two-pane declaration, a native seat and the surface ids the
parity ledger checks against the source.
::

::app-shell[layout=adaptive desktop=panels tablet=panels mobile=tabs panes=two panes-at=tablet shortcuts="mod+1=#surfy mod+2=#cloud mod+3=#tasks mod+4=#terminal mod+5=#messages mod+k=openSearch mod+w=closeTab" surface=chrome.shell]

::: toolbar[title="CloudSurf" surface=chrome.topbar]
- button[label="Search" icon=search action=openSearch focus=1]
- separator
- button[label="New" icon=plus action=openCreate key=mod+n focus=2]
- button[label="Share" icon=share action=shareDoc reveal=hover key="mod+shift+s"]
:::

::: sidebar[position=left collapsible=false width="0 44 44" surface=chrome.navbar pane=start]
::::row[icon=sparkles href=#surfy focus=3]
Surfy
::::
::::row[icon=cloud href=#cloud focus=4]
Cloud
::::
::::row[icon=checkmark.circle href=#tasks focus=5]
Tasks
::::
::::row[icon=terminal href=#terminal focus=6 native=terminal surface=panel.terminal]
Terminal
::::
::::row[icon=message href=#messages focus=7]
Messages
::::
:::

::: panel-slot[role=navigator kind=surfy parks=true surface=panel.surfy pane=start]
:::

